      - {x: 0.75, y: 0.71}
      energized: 0
      color: {r: 1, g: 0.71, b: 0.31, a: 1}
  - title: 02 / Remove the failed radiator
    explanation: Vent the coolant loop, release all fasteners and confirm a supported
      grip before moving the old radiator.
    caption: "ISOLATE  \u2022  UNBOLT  \u2022  CRADLE"
    parts:
    - id: input
      kind: 9
      position: {x: 0.18, y: 0.71}
      label: ISOLATE
      color: {r: 0.18, g: 0.86, b: 0.94, a: 1}
    - id: tracking
      kind: 9
      position: {x: 0.71, y: 0.71}
      label: GRIP
      color: {r: 1, g: 0.71, b: 0.31, a: 1}
    - id: output
      kind: 9
      position: {x: 0.82, y: 0.71}
      label: EXTRACT
      color: {r: 0.18, g: 0.86, b: 0.94, a: 1}
    wires:
    - points:
      - {x: 0.25, y: 0.71}
      - {x: 0.43, y: 0.71}
      energized: 0
      color: {r: 0.18, g: 0.86, b: 0.94, a: 1}
    - points:
      - {x: 0.71, y: 0.71}
      - {x: 0.75, y: 0.71}
      energized: 0
      color: {r: 1, g: 0.71, b: 0.31, a: 1}
  - title: 03 / Fit and cool
    explanation: Fetch the new radiator, settle the slide, torque the fasteners and
      test the pressurized loop and cooling trend.
    caption: "INSTALL  \u2022  TORQUE  \u2022  TEST FLOW"
    parts:
    - id: input
      kind: 9
      position: {x: 0.18, y: 0.71}
      label: ALIGN
      color: {r: 0.18, g: 0.86, b: 0.94, a: 1}
    - id: tracking
      kind: 9
      position: {x: 0.71, y: 0.71}
      label: FASTEN
      color: {r: 1, g: 0.71, b: 0.31, a: 1}
    - id: output
      kind: 9
      position: {x: 0.82, y: 0.71}
      label: COOL
      color: {r: 0.18, g: 0.86, b: 0.94, a: 1}
    wires:
    - points:
      - {x: 0.25, y: 0.71}
      - {x: 0.43, y: 0.71}
      energized: 0
      color: {r: 0.18, g: 0.86, b: 0.94, a: 1}
    - points:
